{
  "schema_version": "0.1",
  "note": "Reviewed axis and representation declarations (decision D9). These replace axis_names(), which matched substrings in profile names: anything containing 'volume' was given image axes, so stroke volume and volume of distribution became pictures, while CT and MRI volumes got two axes for three-dimensional data. Each axis carries a name and what it indexes. Prepared with AI assistance from the pre-review; every entry still needs its domain reviewer.",
  "fields": {
    "axes": "The axes in order. null means the value is scalar and the profile must not require axes. 'port-declared' means the rank varies and the port declares each axis with its meaning.",
    "kinds": "Narrows the allowed representation kinds for this profile.",
    "requires": "Extra items this profile must require because of its structure. Per-axis items (dimensions.axes[].unit and the like) cannot be required yet: dimensions.axes is an ordered list of names, so a per-axis requirement would overwrite it. Making axes carry objects is a D9 follow-up."
  },
